- op: discuss  # 339c
  at: '2026-07-06T04:22:51Z'  # 339c
  by: agent  # 339c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 339c
  clock: 6  # 339c
  nonce: 339c  # 339c
  message: "Priority P2 -> P3. Basis (explicitly NOT 'work stopped' - attention is not a priority signal): the scoped stdlib-builtin shadow fix (dev e278e0b85d) closed the COMMON, high-collision-risk case - dict/list/set/str/... are inherited broadly with a large method-collision surface, the frequent part. The remaining violation is narrower and partly benign: (a) a GENERIC 3rd-party/ORM external base shadowing an in-tree ANCESTOR method - still a confidently-wrong edge (worst FP class per-instance) BUT it requires a genuine NAME COLLISION between the external-base method and an in-tree ANCESTOR method (the class's own method is exempt) with the external ahead in MRO, so lower frequency; (b) Site-3 inherited-field, mechanical (same helper, one call site); (c) multi-level / [Mixin, builtin, Mixin2] interleave, which are UNDER-suppression - SAFE (never emit a wrong edge, only miss a shadow). RE-PROMOTE TRIGGER (evidence-based correction path): if a BROAD bakeoff on framework-heavy Python repos (Django/DRF/Wagtail) surfaces this as a real dead-code/taint FP driver, restore P2 and extend the catalog to well-known ORM bases (the design option-a, bakeoff-gated to avoid over-suppression). Per-instance severity unchanged (confidently-wrong); the demotion reflects reduced frequency/scope after the scoped fix and is reversible on measured evidence, NOT a judgement that the residual is fine."  # 339c
